  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal word used in military, governmental, and organizational hierarchies. Implies that the order comes from a recognized authority and carries the expectation of compliance. Can function as a suru verb ({指令|しれい}する = to issue a directive), though the noun usage is more common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {指令|しれい}を{出|だ}す: to issue an order\n- {指令|しれい}に{従|したが}う: to follow an order\n- {指令|しれい}{系統|けいとう}: chain of command\n- {避難|ひなん}{指令|しれい}: evacuation order\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {命令|めいれい}: order, command (more general, can be personal)\n- {指示|しじ}: instruction, direction (less forceful, more guidance-oriented)",
